# Design notes vs help verbiage (always)

**Served pages must not ship design notes.** Help `?` bodies, FloqAi repository bodies, visible status copy, and HTML comments on Pages must be **operator/patron facing** only.

## Where design decisions live

Put routing contracts, hash defaults, auth resume order, partition flag matrices, “never put `?v=` on Display”, packaging vs Firestore precedence, and agent FIX PROMPTs in:

`.cursor/rules/design-notes-*.mdc`

(or an existing domain always-apply rule such as `screen-datapoints.mdc` / `satellite-session-auth.mdc`).

Code may use a **one-line reference** only:

```js
// Design notes: .cursor/rules/design-notes-master-admin-entity-mgmt.mdc
```

Never paste the design paragraph into `data-floqr-help-body`, `floqai-help-repository.js` `body:`, or UI tooltips.

## Help verbiage (allowed)

What the signed-in person needs to **do or understand** on that screen (how to request SOS2FA, what Email/SMS means, retention). No hash catalogs, no “if signed out then resume then SOS2FA” architecture essays unless that sentence is the user’s next action on *this* screen.

## Checklist before commit

- [ ] New product decision written under `design-notes-*.mdc` (or domain rule)
- [ ] Help / FloqAi body has no design-note paragraph
- [ ] `floqai-help-repository.js` mirrors the short help only
- [ ] No HTML/JS comment blocks that restate the design essay — reference the rule file instead
